      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "$$\n{{\\sqrt{2}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{1-2=1}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\sqrt{2}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{1-2=1}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
